# eager_runtime's calibration artifacts (trained regressor .pkl files and
# their accompanying manifest/hardware-profile .json) must round-trip
# byte-for-byte. Without this, Windows checkouts with core.autocrlf=true
# silently rewrite every lone LF inside the binary .pkl data into CRLF,
# inflating each file and breaking its recorded sha256/size -- which
# runtime_manifest.py's own validation then (correctly) reports as a
# corrupted install. Confirmed real: git's own blob for one such .pkl is
# byte-identical to the manifest's recorded size; only the Windows checkout
# copy was inflated.
orchestrator/eager_runtime/targets/** -text
